body.proof_tex:
Fix \(N\in\mathbb N\) and \(s_N\in(0,1]\) such that \(\mathcal P_N(s_N)\ne\varnothing\).  The estimator \(\widehat\mu\) is the everywhere-defined measurable estimator in \(\operatorname{def:pca-estimator}\).  By \(\operatorname{lem:pca-upper}\),
\[
\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_N(s_N)}
\mathbb E_P L\{\widehat\mu,\mu(P)\}
\le K\min\{1,(Ns_N^2)^{-1}\}.
\]
Because the infimum over all measurable estimators is no larger than the risk of this particular estimator,
\[
\inf_{\widetilde\mu}\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_N(s_N)}
\mathbb E_P L\{\widetilde\mu,\mu(P)\}
\le
\sup_{P\in\mathcal P_N(s_N)}
\mathbb E_P L\{\widehat\mu,\mu(P)\}.
\]
Combining the two displays and taking \(C_0=K\) proves the asserted unconditional upper bound.  No testing-pair, target-separation, or Kullback--Leibler premise is used.
